  "id": "COMPOUND:41859 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Chaetomugilin D and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately interact with this complex. Chaetomugilin D is directly linked to LoVo, a cell line that is a target of 3-Hydroxy-7A-Methyl-1Ah-Naphtho[2,3-B]Oxirene-2,7-Dione and Furanocembranoid 2, both of which have been shown to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Additionally, cortisol, another compound that targets LoVo, also interacts with the same complex. This suggests that Chaetomugilin D may act through a pathway that leads to the activation or inhibition of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially through the modulation of downstream targets like LoVo. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, indicating a possible role for Chaetomugilin D in influencing the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
